#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:413
msgid ""
"Downsample the scene to a small buffer, blur it, overlay additively. "
"Creates soft glow around bright areas. This is the standard generative "
"art bloom technique."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:447
msgid "**Tuning:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:448
msgid "Downsample ratio (1/4 is standard, 1/8 for softer, 1/2 for tighter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:449
msgid "Blur radius (4-8 typical, higher = wider glow)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:450
msgid "Tint alpha (40-120, controls glow intensity)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:451
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Update bloom every N frames to save perf: `if (frameCount % 2 === 0) { "
"... }`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:453
msgid ""
"**Common mistake:** Forgetting `blendMode(BLEND)` after the ADD pass — "
"everything drawn after will be additive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:455
msgid "Trail Buffer Brightness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:457
msgid ""
"Trail accumulation via `createGraphics()` + semi-transparent fade rect is"
" the standard technique for particle trails, but **trails are always "
"dimmer than you expect**. The fade rect's alpha compounds "
"multiplicatively every frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:471
msgid ""
"**The trap:** You set alpha=5 for long trails, but particle strokes at "
"alpha=30 are invisible because they fade before accumulating enough "
"density. Either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:472
msgid "**Boost stroke alpha** to 80-150 (not the intuitive 20-40)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:473
msgid "**Reduce fade alpha** but accept shorter trails"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-effects.md:474
msgid ""
"**Use additive blending** for the strokes: bright particles accumulate, "
"dim ones stay dark"
msgstr ""

